lmcache: start the MP worker heartbeat at KV-cache registration

What: LMCacheMPWorkerAdapter.register_kv_caches() starts the heartbeat thread,
  instead of the first STORE/RETRIEVE/event poll doing so; the two comments
  that described the lazy start are updated.
Why: a vLLM worker that serves no full-chunk prompt within
  --worker-registration-grace-seconds (3600 s) of registering is reaped while
  alive (pinged=False), and PING always returns True, so it never re-registers
  and every later STORE is rejected (c4130, 2026-11-04;
  docs/upstream/lmcache-heartbeat-issue.md).
Upstream-files: lmcache/integration/vllm/vllm_multi_process_adapter.py (LMCache sdist)
Kill-switch: none (build-time); workaround extraArgs --worker-registration-grace-seconds
Tests: build-time apply + ast.parse; hardware check 6 pending
Upstream-status: candidate (draft issue, not filed)

